{"title":"2020 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Pattern_of_the_Rows)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Pattern of the Rows)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Pattern_of_the_Bands)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Pattern of the Bands)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Pattern_of_the_Bands)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Pattern of the Bands)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Brute_Force)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Brute Force)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Summation_Notation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Summation Notation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Quick)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Quick)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_7_(Fast_Pattern_Recognition)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 7 (Fast Pattern Recognition)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_NiuniuMaths_(Easy_to_understand!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by NiuniuMaths (Easy to understand!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_understand_the_problem!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(🚀Under_2_min🚀)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (🚀Under 2 min🚀)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_The_Learning_Royal\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by The Learning Royal</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_North_America_Math_Contest_Go_Go_Go\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by North America Math Contest Go Go Go</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_STEMbreezy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by STEMbreezy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-17\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheNeuralMathAcademy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">17</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheNeuralMathAcademy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-18\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">18</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three hexagons of increasing size are shown below. Suppose the dot pattern continues so that each successive hexagon contains one more band of dots. How many dots are in the next hexagon?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/1/381ea96ddcbeccb0522187fcd4a41c78bd9c8364.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] // diagram by SirCalcsALot, edited by MRENTHUSIASM size(250); path p = scale(0.8)*unitcircle; pair[] A; pen grey1 = rgb(100/256, 100/256, 100/256); pen grey2 = rgb(183/256, 183/256, 183/256); for (int i=0; i&lt;7; ++i) { A[i] = rotate(60*i)*(1,0);} path hex = A[0]--A[1]--A[2]--A[3]--A[4]--A[5]--cycle; fill(p,grey1); draw(scale(1.25)*hex,black+linewidth(1.25)); pair S = 6A[0]+2A[1]; fill(shift(S)*p,grey1); for (int i=0; i&lt;6; ++i) { fill(shift(S+2*A[i])*p,grey2);} draw(shift(S)*scale(3.25)*hex,black+linewidth(1.25)); pair T = 16A[0]+4A[1]; fill(shift(T)*p,grey1); for (int i=0; i&lt;6; ++i) {   fill(shift(T+2*A[i])*p,grey2);  fill(shift(T+4*A[i])*p,grey1);  fill(shift(T+2*A[i]+2*A[i+1])*p,grey1); } draw(shift(T)*scale(5.25)*hex,black+linewidth(1.25)); [/asy]\" width=\"418\" height=\"158\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/5/bd565a87ea030c83de50f3e05dfbeb33d0a6a813.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }35 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }37 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) }39 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) }43 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) }49$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"398\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Pattern_of_the_Rows.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Pattern_of_the_Rows)\">Solution 1 (Pattern of the Rows)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Pattern of the Rows)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Looking at the rows of each hexagon, we see that the first hexagon has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dot, the second has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/c/3bceacd1c7754c02e533aa815614cbeab483fa76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2+3+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"71\" height=\"14\" /> dots, and the third has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f964f4956f71be70aafd0d3ecf9bc098c2b0eb80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3+4+5+4+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"133\" height=\"14\" /> dots. Given the way the hexagons are constructed, it is clear that this pattern continues. Hence, the fourth hexagon has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/2/9920a57d4439e77acf4a5d3d736a6cf001e336cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+5+6+7+6+5+4=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }37}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"286\" height=\"28\" /> dots.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Pattern_of_the_Bands.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Pattern_of_the_Bands)\">Solution 2 (Pattern of the Bands)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Pattern of the Bands)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The dots in the next hexagon have four bands. From innermost to outermost:\n</p>\n<ol style=\"margin-left: 1.5em;\">\n  <li>The first band has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dot.</li><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n  </p><li>The second band has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dots: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dot at each vertex of the hexagon.</li><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n  </p><li>The third band has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/5/0453ffaa1b989f0890eba0c1dce2a614d295951f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+6\\cdot1=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" /> dots: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dot at each vertex of the hexagon and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> other dot on each edge of the hexagon.</li><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n  </p><li>The fourth band has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/b/c8b03b7c3986d36647b4f5e1fe1ba6e3afc61c20.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6+6\\cdot2=18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"107\" height=\"15\" /> dots: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dot at each vertex of the hexagon and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> other dots on each edge of the hexagon.</li><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p></ol>\n<p>Together, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/3/ef3cfb2ddf103e45d7f06c04095d53ccb569098a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+6+12+18=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }37}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"217\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Pattern_of_the_Bands.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Pattern_of_the_Bands)\">Solution 3 (Pattern of the Bands)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Pattern of the Bands)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The first hexagon has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dot, the second hexagon has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/c/55c2e51ab0f15889defecd8e444222f43d5cf604.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"40\" height=\"14\" /> dots, the third hexagon has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/4/e5445b2a6484699d5d744a05625c84f4424fe4ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+6+12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"80\" height=\"14\" /> dots, and so on. The pattern continues since to go from hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> to hexagon <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5060e6e853cd9417ac26f5ed2178d3c860519e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" /> we add a new band of dots around the outside of the existing ones, with each side of the band having side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/7/7d711c9140c4dca21c6abc89fc562bccec73c08a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> Thus, the number of dots added is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/2/362a480a033366928a560965c49a94bfc1bb1cc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6(n+1)-6 = 6n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"140\" height=\"18\" /> (we subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as each of the corner hexagons in the band is counted as part of two sides.). We therefore predict that the fourth hexagon has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/1/6b1f84a6886fbc10a1d15b374a7516f48cb51d37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+6+12+18=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }37}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"210\" height=\"28\" /> dots.\n</p><p><u><b>Remark</b></u>\n</p><p>For positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/4/c54e7152acd659788861f0453ac195c635e0a005.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/5/7959d34399ed5624538871f01af487ebd831572c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> denote the number of dots in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />th hexagon. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/c/03c7aef4631c16fd3b1fdfa2dca975c5cf383d9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_1=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/6/bf6775015d863d3b61a4f3724deda43ee0b6c249.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_{n+1}=h_n+6n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/3/b33c19f0809fac3fab29f824268f620ce1db5d72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_2=7,h_3=19,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/a/70ad9ee3bb1ad67dac684704191da7632216a3ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_4=37.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Brute_Force.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Brute_Force)\">Solution 4 (Brute Force)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Brute Force)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the full diagram below, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/f/08fdf1fbf8da64fd9b6f395f4a03af1e0ef374ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }37}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"71\" height=\"30\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/243c4c6926d2115e57318afc1d10be789bba3b98.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] // diagram by SirCalcsALot, edited by MRENTHUSIASM size(400); path p = scale(0.8)*unitcircle; pair[] A; pen grey1 = rgb(100/256, 100/256, 100/256); pen grey2 = rgb(183/256, 183/256, 183/256); for (int i=0; i&lt;7; ++i) { A[i] = rotate(60*i)*(1,0);} path hex = A[0]--A[1]--A[2]--A[3]--A[4]--A[5]--cycle; fill(p,grey1); draw(scale(1.25)*hex,black+linewidth(1.25)); pair S = 6A[0]+2A[1]; fill(shift(S)*p,grey1); for (int i=0; i&lt;6; ++i) { fill(shift(S+2*A[i])*p,grey2);} draw(shift(S)*scale(3.25)*hex,black+linewidth(1.25)); pair T = 16A[0]+4A[1]; fill(shift(T)*p,grey1); for (int i=0; i&lt;6; ++i) {   fill(shift(T+2*A[i])*p,grey2);  fill(shift(T+4*A[i])*p,grey1);  fill(shift(T+2*A[i]+2*A[i+1])*p,grey1); } draw(shift(T)*scale(5.25)*hex,black+linewidth(1.25));  pair R = 30A[0]+6A[1]; fill(shift(R)*p,grey1); for (int i=0; i&lt;6; ++i) {   fill(shift(R+2*A[i])*p,grey2);  fill(shift(R+4*A[i])*p,grey1);  fill(shift(R+2*A[i]+2*A[i+1])*p,grey1);  fill(shift(R+6*A[i+1])*p,grey2);  fill(shift(R+2*A[i]+4*A[i+1])*p,grey2);  fill(shift(R+4*A[i]+2*A[i+1])*p,grey2); } draw(shift(R)*scale(7.25)*hex,black+linewidth(1.25)); [/asy]\" width=\"668\" height=\"205\" />\n~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Summation_Notation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Summation_Notation)\">Solution 5 (Summation Notation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Summation Notation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We solve thiss using the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/3/9330498087d6362178b2425bfbac0cb0b5971df5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Sigma Function}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"17\" /> (summation notation).\n</p><p>The sequence starts at:\n\\[\na_1 = 1\n\\]\n</p><p>Each term increases by a growing difference:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\na_2 &amp;= a_1 + 6 = 7 \\\\\na_3 &amp;= a_2 + 12 = 19 \\\\\na_4 &amp;= a_3 + 18 = 37\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\n</p><p>We observe that the difference added at each step forms an arithmetic sequence:  \n\\[\n6,\\, 12,\\, 18,\\, 24,\\, \\dots = 6k \\text{ for } k = 1, 2, 3, \\dots\n\\]\n</p><p>To express this with the \\textbf{Sigma Function}, we write the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-th term as:\n</p><p>a_n = 1 + \\sum_{k=1}^{n-1} 6k\n\\]\n</p><p>This is a standard arithmetic sum, so we use the formula:\n\\[\n\\sum_{k=1}^{n-1} k = \\frac{(n-1)n}{2}\n\\]\n</p><p>Substitute this in:\n\\[\na_n = 1 + 6 \\cdot \\frac{(n-1)n}{2}\n\\]\n</p><p>When we simplify:\n\\[\na_n = 1 + 3n(n - 1)\n\\]\n\\[\n\\boxed{a_n = 1 + 3n(n - 1)}\n\\]\n</p><p>Let’s compute the 4th term using the sigma-based formula:\n\\[\na_4 = 1 + 3 \\cdot 4 \\cdot (4 - 1) = 1 + 3 \\cdot 12 = 1 + 36 = \\boxed{37}\n\\]\nSo the answer is 37.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Quick.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Quick)\">Solution 6 (Quick)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Quick)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that the middle row, which is also the row with the most dots in it, has the same number of dots as the topmost or bottommost row multiplied by 2, then minus one. Since the new hexagon will have four dots at the topmost and bottommost rows, the middle row will have (4*2)-1=7 dots. Also, notice that the rows increase in the number of dots from the topmost to the middle row, then decrease from the middle row to the bottommost row by 1. So, noticing these patterns, the amount of dots in the next hexagon is simply <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/2/9920a57d4439e77acf4a5d3d736a6cf001e336cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+5+6+7+6+5+4=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }37}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"286\" height=\"28\" /> dots.~Evžen D.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_7_.28Fast_Pattern_Recognition.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_7_(Fast_Pattern_Recognition)\">Solution 7 (Fast Pattern Recognition)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 7 (Fast Pattern Recognition)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The first hexagon has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dot in it. The second hexagon has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> dots in it. The third hexagon has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> dots on it. From the first to the second, we add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hexagons. From the second to the third, we add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> hexagons. Therefore, recognizing the pattern, from the third to the fourth case, we have to add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> dots to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efbfe273946ff9f971c5eab331ca39caa6fdf7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> we already have, resulting in our answer of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/2/2d23b3ff0b02f9fabb46cfd5a5767d1cee66f257.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }37}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"64\" height=\"28\" /> dots.\n</p><p>~BryBro7\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_NiuniuMaths_.28Easy_to_understand.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_NiuniuMaths_(Easy_to_understand!)\">Video Solution by NiuniuMaths (Easy to understand!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by NiuniuMaths (Easy to understand!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8hgK6rESdek&amp;t=9s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8hgK6rESdek&amp;t=9s</a>\n</p><p>~NiuniuMaths\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_.28First_understand_the_problem.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_understand_the_problem!!!)\">Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/UnVo6jZ3Wnk?si=bKY7jHWZFGeYKoM6&amp;t=324\">https://youtu.be/UnVo6jZ3Wnk?si=bKY7jHWZFGeYKoM6&amp;t=324</a>\n</p><p>~Math-X\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28.F0.9F.9A.80Under_2_min.F0.9F.9A.80.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(🚀Under_2_min🚀)\">Video Solution (🚀Under 2 min🚀)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (🚀Under 2 min🚀)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\